IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 23AA to 23E: delegation, statutory bodies, temporary appointments, pay before commencement, the Governor's power over remuneration.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.

§ `s 23AA: delegation`

DECLARE `Delegate of a function or power` IS ONE OF
    `a person by name`
    `the holder of a particular office or position by reference to the title of the office or position concerned, whether or not the office or position is vacant at the time of the delegation`
    `some other delegate`

-- src:463 | (1) If an Act confers a power on a person to delegate a function or power, the person may, in accordance with the Act, delegate the function or power to –
-- src:465 | (a) a person by name; or
-- src:467 | (b) the holder of a particular office or position by reference to the title of the office or position concerned, whether or not the office or position is vacant at the time of the delegation.
@ref s 23AA(1) (src:463-467)
GIVEN `an Act confers a power on a person to delegate a function or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegation is in accordance with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      delegate IS A `Delegate of a function or power`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(1): the person may delegate the function or power to` `an Act confers a power on a person to delegate a function or power` `the delegation is in accordance with the Act` delegate MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`an Act confers a power on a person to delegate a function or power`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"
           IF (NOT (`the delegation is in accordance with the Act`)) OR delegate EQUALS `some other delegate` THEN NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Scope of a delegation` IS ONE OF
    `general`
    `limited`

-- src:471 | (a) may be general or limited; and
@ref s 23AA(2)(a) (src:471)
GIVEN scope IS A `Scope of a delegation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(2)(a): a delegation may be` scope MEANS
    CONSIDER scope
    WHEN `general` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `limited` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:473 | (b) must be in, or evidenced by, writing signed by the delegator or, if the delegator is a body, by a person authorized by the body for that purpose; and
@ref s 23AA(2)(b) (src:473)
GIVEN `the delegator is a body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegation is in, or evidenced by, writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is signed by the delegator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is signed by a person authorized by the body for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(2)(b): the delegation is in the form it must be in` `the delegator is a body` `the delegation is in, or evidenced by, writing` `the writing is signed by the delegator` `the writing is signed by a person authorized by the body for that purpose` MEANS
    `the delegation is in, or evidenced by, writing`
    AND (IF `the delegator is a body` THEN `the writing is signed by a person authorized by the body for that purpose` ELSE `the writing is signed by the delegator`)

-- src:475 | (c) may be revoked, wholly or partly, by the delegator.
@ref s 23AA(2)(c) (src:475)
GIVEN `the person revoking is the delegator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(2)(c): the delegation may be revoked, wholly or partly` `the person revoking is the delegator` MEANS
    IF `the person revoking is the delegator` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:477 | (3) A delegated function or power may be exercised only in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject.
@ref s 23AA(3) (src:477)
GIVEN `the exercise is in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(3): the delegated function or power may be exercised` `the exercise is in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject` MEANS
    IF `the exercise is in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:479 | (4) A delegated function or power that is duly exercised by a delegate is to be taken to have been exercised by the delegator.
@ref s 23AA(4) (src:479)
GIVEN `the delegated function or power is duly exercised by a delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(4): the exercise is taken to have been an exercise by the delegator` `the delegated function or power is duly exercised by a delegate` MEANS
    IF `the delegated function or power is duly exercised by a delegate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:483 | (a) the delegation does not cease to have effect merely because the person who was the particular officer or the holder of the particular office or position when the function or power was delegated ceases to be that officer or the holder of that office or position; and
@ref s 23AA(5)(a) (src:483)
GIVEN `the function or power is delegated to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who was the officer or holder when the function or power was delegated ceases to be that officer or holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(5)(a): the delegation does not cease to have effect merely because of the change` `the function or power is delegated to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position` `the person who was the officer or holder when the function or power was delegated ceases to be that officer or holder` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the function or power is delegated to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"
           IF NOT (`the person who was the officer or holder when the function or power was delegated ceases to be that officer or holder`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:485 | (b) the function or power may be performed or exercised by the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office or position concerned.
@ref s 23AA(5)(b) (src:485)
GIVEN `the function or power is delegated to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is for the time being occupying or acting in the office or position concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(5)(b): the person may perform or exercise the function or power` `the function or power is delegated to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position` `the person is for the time being occupying or acting in the office or position concerned` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the function or power is delegated to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"
           IF NOT (`the person is for the time being occupying or acting in the office or position concerned`) THEN NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:489 | (a) the delegation does not cease to have effect merely because the person who was the particular officer or the holder of the particular office or position when the function or power was delegated ceases to be that officer or the holder of that office or position; and
@ref s 23AA(5A)(a) (src:489)
GIVEN `the function or power is delegated by a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who was the officer or holder when the function or power was delegated ceases to be that officer or holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(5A)(a): the delegation does not cease to have effect merely because of the change` `the function or power is delegated by a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position` `the person who was the officer or holder when the function or power was delegated ceases to be that officer or holder` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the function or power is delegated by a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"
           IF NOT (`the person who was the officer or holder when the function or power was delegated ceases to be that officer or holder`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:491 | (b) the authority of the delegate to exercise that power or perform that function continues until that authority is terminated by notice in writing by the particular officer or the holder for the time being of the relevant office or position.
@ref s 23AA(5A)(b) (src:491)
GIVEN `the function or power is delegated by a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has been terminated by notice in writing by the particular officer or the holder for the time being of the relevant office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(5A)(b): the authority of the delegate continues` `the function or power is delegated by a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position` `the authority has been terminated by notice in writing by the particular officer or the holder for the time being of the relevant office or position` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the function or power is delegated by a particular officer or the holder of a particular office or position`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"
           IF `the authority has been terminated by notice in writing by the particular officer or the holder for the time being of the relevant office or position` THEN JUST FALSE   -- "until": after the termination
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:493 | (6) A function or power that has been delegated may, notwithstanding the delegation, be exercised by the delegator.
@ref s 23AA(6) (src:493)
GIVEN `the function or power has been delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(6): the delegator may, notwithstanding the delegation, exercise the function or power` `the function or power has been delegated` MEANS
    IF `the function or power has been delegated` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:495 | (7) This section applies to a sub-delegation of a function or power in the same way as it applies to a delegation of a function or power, but only so far as the Act that authorizes the delegation of the function or power also authorizes the sub-delegation of the function or power.
@ref s 23AA(7) (src:495)
GIVEN `the function or power is sub-delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act that authorizes the delegation also authorizes the sub-delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(7): this section applies to the sub-delegation` `the function or power is sub-delegated` `the Act that authorizes the delegation also authorizes the sub-delegation` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the function or power is sub-delegated`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the Act that authorizes the delegation also authorizes the sub-delegation` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:497 | (8) In all courts and before all persons acting judicially, an instrument purporting to be executed by a delegate in the capacity as a delegate is to be received in evidence as if it were an instrument executed by the delegator and is to be taken to be an instrument executed by the delegator.
@ref s 23AA(8) (src:497)
GIVEN `the proceeding is in a court or before a person acting judicially` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument purports to be executed by a delegate in the capacity as a delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AA(8): the instrument is received in evidence as if executed by the delegator and is taken to be an instrument executed by the delegator` `the proceeding is in a court or before a person acting judicially` `the instrument purports to be executed by a delegate in the capacity as a delegate` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is in a court or before a person acting judicially` AND `the instrument purports to be executed by a delegate in the capacity as a delegate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

