§ `s 23AAB: power to delegate includes power to authorise`

-- src:499 | 23AAB. Power to delegate includes power to authorise
-- src:501 | If in an Act a power to delegate a function or power is conferred on a person, the power to delegate the function or power includes a power to authorise another person to perform the function or exercise the power on behalf of the person giving the authorisation and sections 23AA and 23A apply in respect of the authorisation as if it were a delegation.
@ref s 23AAB (src:499-501)
GIVEN `in an Act a power to delegate a function or power is conferred on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AAB: the power to delegate includes a power to authorise another person to perform the function or exercise the power on behalf of the person giving the authorisation` `in an Act a power to delegate a function or power is conferred on a person` MEANS
    IF `in an Act a power to delegate a function or power is conferred on a person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"

GIVEN `in an Act a power to delegate a function or power is conferred on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another person is authorised under that power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AAB: sections 23AA and 23A apply in respect of the authorisation as if it were a delegation` `in an Act a power to delegate a function or power is conferred on a person` `another person is authorised under that power` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`in an Act a power to delegate a function or power is conferred on a person`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"
           IF NOT (`another person is authorised under that power`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 23AAB: the power to delegate includes a power to authorise another person to perform the function or exercise the power on behalf of the person giving the authorisation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23AAB: the power to delegate includes a power to authorise another person to perform the function or exercise the power on behalf of the person giving the authorisation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23AAB: sections 23AA and 23A apply in respect of the authorisation as if it were a delegation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23AAB: sections 23AA and 23A apply in respect of the authorisation as if it were a delegation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23AAB: sections 23AA and 23A apply in respect of the authorisation as if it were a delegation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 23A: exercise of certain powers and functions by a delegate`

DECLARE `Person whose opinion, belief or state of mind governs` IS ONE OF
    `the delegate`
    `the person who delegated`

-- src:505 | (1) Where, under an Act, the exercise of a power or function by a person is dependent upon the opinion, belief, or state of mind of that person in relation to a matter and that power or function has been delegated in pursuance of that Act, that power or function may be exercised by the delegate upon the opinion, belief, or state of mind of the delegate in relation to that matter.
@ref s 23A(1) (src:505)
GIVEN `the exercise of a power or function by a person under an Act is dependent upon the opinion, belief or state of mind of that person in relation to a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power or function has been delegated in pursuance of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Person whose opinion, belief or state of mind governs`)
`s 23A(1): the opinion, belief or state of mind upon which the delegate may exercise the power or function is that of` `the exercise of a power or function by a person under an Act is dependent upon the opinion, belief or state of mind of that person in relation to a matter` `the power or function has been delegated in pursuance of that Act` MEANS
    IF `the exercise of a power or function by a person under an Act is dependent upon the opinion, belief or state of mind of that person in relation to a matter` AND `the power or function has been delegated in pursuance of that Act`
    THEN JUST `the delegate`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:507 | (2) Where the operation of a provision of an Act is dependent upon the opinion, belief, or state of mind in relation to a matter of a person specified in that Act and any of the powers or functions of that person have been delegated, in pursuance of that Act, to some other person, that provision may operate upon the opinion, belief, or state of mind of the delegate in relation to that matter.
@ref s 23A(2) (src:507)
GIVEN `the operation of a provision of an Act is dependent upon the opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to a matter of a person specified in that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of the powers or functions of that person have been delegated, in pursuance of that Act, to some other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Person whose opinion, belief or state of mind governs`)
`s 23A(2): the opinion, belief or state of mind upon which the provision may operate is that of` `the operation of a provision of an Act is dependent upon the opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to a matter of a person specified in that Act` `any of the powers or functions of that person have been delegated, in pursuance of that Act, to some other person` MEANS
    IF `the operation of a provision of an Act is dependent upon the opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to a matter of a person specified in that Act` AND `any of the powers or functions of that person have been delegated, in pursuance of that Act, to some other person`
    THEN JUST `the delegate`
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 23A(1): the opinion, belief or state of mind upon which the delegate may exercise the power or function is that of` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the delegate`
#ASSERT `s 23A(1): the opinion, belief or state of mind upon which the delegate may exercise the power or function is that of` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(1): the opinion, belief or state of mind upon which the delegate may exercise the power or function is that of` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(2): the opinion, belief or state of mind upon which the provision may operate is that of` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the delegate`
#ASSERT `s 23A(2): the opinion, belief or state of mind upon which the provision may operate is that of` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(2): the opinion, belief or state of mind upon which the provision may operate is that of` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 23AB: formation of statutory bodies`

-- src:509 | 23AB. Formation of statutory bodies
-- src:511 | Where, by or under any Act, there is required to be, or there may be, established, constituted, or appointed any board, commission, committee, or other body of persons (whether incorporated or unincorporated) and the Governor is satisfied that it is necessary for that body to enter upon its functions forthwith but that it is not practicable for the full number of members of the Board to be elected or appointed within a reasonable time he may declare that Board to be duly established, constituted, or appointed if there are sufficient persons appointed or elected as members thereof to constitute a quorum at a meeting of that body; and on the making of that declaration that body shall, accordingly, be deemed to be duly constituted, established, or appointed.
@ref s 23AB declaration (src:509-511)
GIVEN `by or under an Act a board, commission, committee or other body of persons is required to be, or may be, established, constituted or appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Governor is satisfied that it is necessary for the body to enter upon its functions forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Governor is satisfied that it is not practicable for the full number of members to be elected or appointed within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons appointed or elected as members` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members that constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the body` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AB: the Governor may declare the body duly established, constituted or appointed` `by or under an Act a board, commission, committee or other body of persons is required to be, or may be, established, constituted or appointed` `the Governor is satisfied that it is necessary for the body to enter upon its functions forthwith` `the Governor is satisfied that it is not practicable for the full number of members to be elected or appointed within a reasonable time` `the number of persons appointed or elected as members` `the number of members that constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the body` MEANS
    IF `by or under an Act a board, commission, committee or other body of persons is required to be, or may be, established, constituted or appointed`
       AND `the Governor is satisfied that it is necessary for the body to enter upon its functions forthwith`
       AND `the Governor is satisfied that it is not practicable for the full number of members to be elected or appointed within a reasonable time`
       AND `the number of persons appointed or elected as members` AT LEAST `the number of members that constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where", or the "if" about the quorum

GIVEN `the Governor has made the declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23AB: on the declaration the body is deemed to be duly constituted, established or appointed` `the Governor has made the declaration` MEANS
    IF `the Governor has made the declaration` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- "on the making of that declaration", read as "upon"

#ASSERT `s 23AB: the Governor may declare the body duly established, constituted or appointed` TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23AB: the Governor may declare the body duly established, constituted or appointed` TRUE TRUE TRUE 7 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23AB: the Governor may declare the body duly established, constituted or appointed` TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23AB: the Governor may declare the body duly established, constituted or appointed` FALSE TRUE TRUE 5 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23AB: the Governor may declare the body duly established, constituted or appointed` TRUE FALSE TRUE 5 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23AB: the Governor may declare the body duly established, constituted or appointed` TRUE TRUE FALSE 5 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23AB: on the declaration the body is deemed to be duly constituted, established or appointed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23AB: on the declaration the body is deemed to be duly constituted, established or appointed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 23B: temporary appointments to vacancies on boards and the like`

-- src:515 | (1) Where –
-- src:517 | (a) by or under an Act, there is established, constituted, or appointed any board, commission, committee, or other body of persons (whether incorporated or unincorporated) consisting of or including any members to whose appointment nomination by any person or election by any persons is a condition precedent; and
-- src:519 | (b) it becomes necessary for any reason to replace a member of the board, commission, committee, or body and it appears to the Governor that it is not practicable for a nomination or an election to be made or held within a reasonable time –
-- src:521 | the Governor may, by proclamation setting out the circumstances requiring action, appoint some person to hold office as a member of the board, commission, committee, or body until the vacancy can be regularly filled; but, where the nomination or election is required to be made by a body of persons having a general committee, committee of management, executive committee, or other like institution that can conveniently be consulted, the Governor shall, if it is reasonably practicable so to do, obtain the assent of that committee or institution to the appointment.
@ref s 23B(1) appointment (src:515-521)
GIVEN `by or under an Act a board, commission, committee or other body of persons is established, constituted or appointed, consisting of or including members to whose appointment nomination by any person or election by any persons is a condition precedent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it becomes necessary for any reason to replace a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Governor that it is not practicable for a nomination or an election to be made or held within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proclamation sets out the circumstances requiring action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23B(1): the Governor may, by proclamation, appoint a person to hold office as a member until the vacancy can be regularly filled` `by or under an Act a board, commission, committee or other body of persons is established, constituted or appointed, consisting of or including members to whose appointment nomination by any person or election by any persons is a condition precedent` `it becomes necessary for any reason to replace a member` `it appears to the Governor that it is not practicable for a nomination or an election to be made or held within a reasonable time` `the proclamation sets out the circumstances requiring action` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`by or under an Act a board, commission, committee or other body of persons is established, constituted or appointed, consisting of or including members to whose appointment nomination by any person or election by any persons is a condition precedent`
                   AND `it becomes necessary for any reason to replace a member`
                   AND `it appears to the Governor that it is not practicable for a nomination or an election to be made or held within a reasonable time`)
           THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the proclamation sets out the circumstances requiring action`) THEN NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:515 | (1) Where –
-- src:517 | (a) by or under an Act, there is established, constituted, or appointed any board, commission, committee, or other body of persons (whether incorporated or unincorporated) consisting of or including any members to whose appointment nomination by any person or election by any persons is a condition precedent; and
-- src:519 | (b) it becomes necessary for any reason to replace a member of the board, commission, committee, or body and it appears to the Governor that it is not practicable for a nomination or an election to be made or held within a reasonable time –
-- src:521 | the Governor may, by proclamation setting out the circumstances requiring action, appoint some person to hold office as a member of the board, commission, committee, or body until the vacancy can be regularly filled; but, where the nomination or election is required to be made by a body of persons having a general committee, committee of management, executive committee, or other like institution that can conveniently be consulted, the Governor shall, if it is reasonably practicable so to do, obtain the assent of that committee or institution to the appointment.
@ref s 23B(1) assent of the committee (src:515-521)
GIVEN `the nomination or election is required to be made by a body of persons having a general committee, committee of management, executive committee or other like institution that can conveniently be consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonably practicable to obtain the assent of that committee or institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23B(1): the Governor must obtain the assent of the committee or institution to the appointment` `the nomination or election is required to be made by a body of persons having a general committee, committee of management, executive committee or other like institution that can conveniently be consulted` `it is reasonably practicable to obtain the assent of that committee or institution` MEANS
    IF `the nomination or election is required to be made by a body of persons having a general committee, committee of management, executive committee or other like institution that can conveniently be consulted` AND `it is reasonably practicable to obtain the assent of that committee or institution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "where", or the "if" about what is reasonably practicable

DECLARE `Way of questioning a proclamation in a court` IS ONE OF
    `an order of review made under the Judicial Review Act 2000`
    `any other way`

-- src:523 | (2) No proclamation under this section shall be questioned in any court except by an order of review made under the Judicial Review Act 2000; and if on the hearing of the information judgment of ouster is given, all the acts of the person ousted purporting to be done by virtue of his appointment before the date of judgment shall, notwithstanding the judgment of ouster, be deemed to be as valid for all purposes as if he had been lawfully appointed to the board, commission, committee, or body of persons.
@ref s 23B(2) proclamation (src:523)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of questioning a proclamation in a court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23B(2): the proclamation may not be questioned in a court by` way MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `an order of review made under the Judicial Review Act 2000` THEN JUST FALSE   -- the "except" is met
    WHEN `any other way` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:523 | (2) No proclamation under this section shall be questioned in any court except by an order of review made under the Judicial Review Act 2000; and if on the hearing of the information judgment of ouster is given, all the acts of the person ousted purporting to be done by virtue of his appointment before the date of judgment shall, notwithstanding the judgment of ouster, be deemed to be as valid for all purposes as if he had been lawfully appointed to the board, commission, committee, or body of persons.
@ref s 23B(2) acts of the person ousted (src:523)
GIVEN `judgment of ouster is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act purported to be done by virtue of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
      `the day of the judgment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23B(2): the act of the person ousted is deemed to be as valid for all purposes as if the person had been lawfully appointed` `judgment of ouster is given` `the act purported to be done by virtue of the appointment` `the day the act was done` `the day of the judgment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`judgment of ouster is given`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "if"
           IF NOT (`the day the act was done` BELOW `the day of the judgment`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- "before the date of judgment": a period the text fixes
           IF NOT (`the act purported to be done by virtue of the appointment`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 23B(1): the Governor may, by proclamation, appoint a person to hold office as a member until the vacancy can be regularly filled` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23B(1): the Governor may, by proclamation, appoint a person to hold office as a member until the vacancy can be regularly filled` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
