#ASSERT `s 23B(1): the Governor may, by proclamation, appoint a person to hold office as a member until the vacancy can be regularly filled` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23B(1): the Governor may, by proclamation, appoint a person to hold office as a member until the vacancy can be regularly filled` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23B(1): the Governor must obtain the assent of the committee or institution to the appointment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23B(1): the Governor must obtain the assent of the committee or institution to the appointment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23B(1): the Governor must obtain the assent of the committee or institution to the appointment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23B(2): the proclamation may not be questioned in a court by` `an order of review made under the Judicial Review Act 2000` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23B(2): the proclamation may not be questioned in a court by` `any other way` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23B(2): the act of the person ousted is deemed to be as valid for all purposes as if the person had been lawfully appointed` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23B(2): the act of the person ousted is deemed to be as valid for all purposes as if the person had been lawfully appointed` TRUE TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23B(2): the act of the person ousted is deemed to be as valid for all purposes as if the person had been lawfully appointed` TRUE TRUE (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23B(2): the act of the person ousted is deemed to be as valid for all purposes as if the person had been lawfully appointed` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23B(2): the act of the person ousted is deemed to be as valid for all purposes as if the person had been lawfully appointed` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 23C: power of statutory bodies to act during vacancies in membership`

-- src:525 | 23C. Power of statutory bodies to act during vacancies in membership
-- src:527 | Where pursuant to any Act there is established, constituted, or appointed any board, commission, committee, or other body of persons (whether incorporated or unincorporated) comprising 2 or more members that Act shall, unless the contrary intention appears therein, be deemed to empower that board, commission, committee, or other body to function, and the members, or persons empowered to act as members thereof, to act, notwithstanding any vacancies in the membership thereof, so long as there are sufficient members to constitute a quorum at a meeting of that board, commission, committee, or other body.
@ref s 23C (src:525-527)
GIVEN `pursuant to an Act a board, commission, committee or other body of persons is established, constituted or appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members the body comprises` IS A NUMBER
      `the contrary intention appears in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members in office` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members that constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the body` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23C: the Act is deemed to empower the body to function, and its members to act, notwithstanding vacancies in the membership` `pursuant to an Act a board, commission, committee or other body of persons is established, constituted or appointed` `the number of members the body comprises` `the contrary intention appears in the Act` `the number of members in office` `the number of members that constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the body` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`pursuant to an Act a board, commission, committee or other body of persons is established, constituted or appointed` AND `the number of members the body comprises` AT LEAST 2) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary intention appears in the Act` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the number of members in office` AT LEAST `the number of members that constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the body` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- "so long as there are sufficient members"

#ASSERT `s 23C: the Act is deemed to empower the body to function, and its members to act, notwithstanding vacancies in the membership` TRUE 5 FALSE 3 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23C: the Act is deemed to empower the body to function, and its members to act, notwithstanding vacancies in the membership` TRUE 5 FALSE 4 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23C: the Act is deemed to empower the body to function, and its members to act, notwithstanding vacancies in the membership` TRUE 5 FALSE 2 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23C: the Act is deemed to empower the body to function, and its members to act, notwithstanding vacancies in the membership` TRUE 5 TRUE 4 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23C: the Act is deemed to empower the body to function, and its members to act, notwithstanding vacancies in the membership` TRUE 2 FALSE 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23C: the Act is deemed to empower the body to function, and its members to act, notwithstanding vacancies in the membership` TRUE 1 FALSE 1 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23C: the Act is deemed to empower the body to function, and its members to act, notwithstanding vacancies in the membership` FALSE 5 FALSE 4 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 23D: payment of persons appointed before commencement of an Act`

-- src:529 | 23D. Payment of persons appointed before commencement of Act
-- src:531 | Where a person is appointed to any office or place under or for the purposes of an Act before the commencement of that Act that person may, during the period between the date of his appointment to that office or place and the date of the commencement of that Act, be paid such remuneration and such sums by way of reimbursement of expenses as he could have been paid if the Act had commenced on the date of his appointment.
@ref s 23D (src:529-531)
GIVEN `a person is appointed to an office or place under or for the purposes of an Act before the commencement of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day of the commencement of the Act` IS A DATE
      `the day the payment is for` IS A DATE
      `the sum` IS A NUMBER
      `the most the person could have been paid if the Act had commenced on the date of the appointment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` `a person is appointed to an office or place under or for the purposes of an Act before the commencement of that Act` `the day of the appointment` `the day of the commencement of the Act` `the day the payment is for` `the sum` `the most the person could have been paid if the Act had commenced on the date of the appointment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a person is appointed to an office or place under or for the purposes of an Act before the commencement of that Act` AND `the day of the appointment` BELOW `the day of the commencement of the Act`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the day the payment is for` AT LEAST `the day of the appointment` AND `the day the payment is for` AT MOST `the day of the commencement of the Act`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- "during the period between": a period the text fixes
           IF `the sum` AT MOST `the most the person could have been paid if the Act had commenced on the date of the appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording: "such sums ... as he could have been paid"

#ASSERT `s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) 100 150 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) 151 150 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) 100 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 2 5 2026) 100 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) 100 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23D: the person may be paid the sum` TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) 100 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 23E: exercise of power of the Governor to approve and the like remuneration of office holders`

DECLARE `Person who exercises the Governor's power over remuneration` IS ONE OF
    `a Minister`
    `a person authorised in writing by the Governor for that purpose`
    `a person authorised by the Governor otherwise than in writing`
    `any other person`

-- src:533 | 23E. Exercise of power of Governor to approve, &c., remuneration of office holders
-- src:535 | Where an Act provides the Governor with the power to approve, determine or otherwise fix the remuneration, expenses or other emoluments payable to the holder of an office, that power may also be exercised by –
-- src:537 | (a) a Minister; or
-- src:539 | (b) any other person authorised in writing by the Governor for that purpose.
@ref s 23E (src:533-539)
GIVEN `an Act provides the Governor with the power to approve, determine or otherwise fix the remuneration, expenses or other emoluments payable to the holder of an office` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Person who exercises the Governor's power over remuneration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23E: the power may also be exercised by` `an Act provides the Governor with the power to approve, determine or otherwise fix the remuneration, expenses or other emoluments payable to the holder of an office` person MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`an Act provides the Governor with the power to approve, determine or otherwise fix the remuneration, expenses or other emoluments payable to the holder of an office`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF person EQUALS `a Minister` OR person EQUALS `a person authorised in writing by the Governor for that purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording

#ASSERT `s 23E: the power may also be exercised by` TRUE `a Minister` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23E: the power may also be exercised by` TRUE `a person authorised in writing by the Governor for that purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23E: the power may also be exercised by` TRUE `a person authorised by the Governor otherwise than in writing` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23E: the power may also be exercised by` TRUE `any other person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23E: the power may also be exercised by` FALSE `a Minister` EQUALS JUST FALSE
